Secretary of State Mike Pompeo will be  in New York City today to meet with  North Korea's top nuclear weapons  negotiator his meeting with kim  youngchul comes at a pivotal time both  countries are working to revive a summit  between President Trump  and North Korean leader Kim jong-un  originally scheduled for next month  Kylie Atwood is at the State Department  Kylie good morning good morning  beyond meetings at the UN this is the  first time in 18 years that a North  Korean official is meeting with a top US  government official on US soil Pompeo is  heading to the White House later today  to talk with President Trump about his  meeting with North Korea's top spy chief  and for Pompeo and kim youngchul this  will be their third time face to face  but both of the previous Huddle's  happened in Pyongyang and this meeting  will inject new momentum into the  negotiating and planning leading up to  that Trump Kim jong-un summit that's  tentatively set to take place in  Singapore on June 12th but nothing is  certain just last week Trump wrote a  letter to Kim jong-un canceling the  meeting  Pompeyo had said that the US team was  getting a lot of dial tones simply  ignored by Kim's regime now mr. Trump  has tweeted that kim gyeong-cheol visit  should be quote a solid response to his  letter and despite this historic meeting  it's a long road ahead just this week  there was a report out that said that it  could take up to 15 years for North  Korea to fully and safely denuclearize  Gayle all right Kylie thank you very  much reporting from Washington for us  today
 

